{"graph_chars": "Chapter Two's Bring It Home returns to the degree. Some people do not hold a bachelor's because tuition is high. Some do not because the full opportunity cost, including years of lost earnings, is too high. That choice lives inside their opportunity set. Before you go, here is the recitation for Chapter Two. Opportunity cost is the value of the next best alternative. It includes time, not only cash. Alphonso's ten dollars buy five burgers or twenty tickets. A burger costs four tickets. Utility diminishes on the margin. Ignore sunk costs. The P P F is curved because opportunity cost rises. Points on the curve are productively efficient. Points inside are wasteful. Allocative efficiency is the mix society wants. Comparative advantage is lower opportunity cost. Brazil sugar, the United States wheat. Positive describes. Normative prescribes. The invisible hand is self-interest that can serve the public. That is Chapter Two.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0645], [0.0645, 0.1291], [0.1291, 0.1936], [0.1936, 0.2582], [0.2582, 0.3227], [0.3227, 0.3873], [0.3873, 0.4518], [0.4518, 0.5164], [0.5164, 0.5809], [0.5809, 0.6454], [0.6454, 0.71], [0.71, 0.7745], [0.7745, 0.8391], [0.8391, 0.9036], [0.9036, 0.9682], [0.9682, 1.0327], [1.0327, 1.0973], [1.0973, 1.1618], [1.1618, 1.2263], [1.2263, 1.2909], [1.2909, 1.3554], [1.3554, 1.42], [1.42, 1.4845], [1.4845, 1.5491], [1.5491, 1.6136], [1.6136, 1.6782], [1.6782, 1.7427], [1.7427, 1.8072], [1.8072, 1.8718], [1.8718, 1.9363], [1.9363, 2.0009], [2.0009, 2.0654], [2.0654, 2.13], [2.13, 2.1945], [2.1945, 2.2591], [2.2591, 2.3236], [2.3236, 2.3881], [2.3881, 2.4527], [2.4527, 2.5172], [2.5172, 2.5818], [2.5818, 2.6463], [2.6463, 2.7109], [2.7109, 2.7754], [2.7754, 2.84], [2.84, 2.9045], [2.9045, 2.969], [2.969, 3.0336], [3.0336, 3.0981], [3.0981, 3.1627], [3.1627, 3.2272], [3.2272, 3.2918], [3.2918, 3.3563], [3.3563, 3.4209], [3.4209, 3.4854], [3.4854, 3.5499], [3.5499, 3.6145], [3.6145, 3.679], [3.679, 3.7436], [3.7436, 3